{{!-- The picture box for a story.

     One aspect ratio everywhere, 3:2, and the space is always
     reserved, so nothing moves on the page when real photography
     arrives later.

     A story without a feature image gets a halftone screened at 45
     degrees, the angle used for the black plate in offset printing.
     It is seeded from the post id, so it is the same picture every
     time a reader sees that story, and it is decoration: it carries
     aria-hidden, no alt text and no caption, and it is never
     presented as a photograph of anything. The headline is the
     meaning; this is the rhythm. --}}

<span class="lc-frame">
    {{#if feature_image}}
        {{> "responsive-image" src=feature_image alt=feature_image_alt sizes=sizes eager=eager}}
    {{else}}
        <canvas data-lc-halftone="{{id}}" data-ratio="3/2" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    {{/if}}
</span>
